Appendix C: Topology Optimisation — SIMP Formulation

C.1 Minimum Compliance and KKT Conditions

Problem C.1 (SIMP Minimum Compliance).
For a design domain discretised into N finite elements,

\begin{aligned}
\min_{\boldsymbol{\rho}} \quad & C(\boldsymbol{\rho}) = \mathbf{F}^\mathsf{T} \mathbf{U} \\
\text{s.t.} \quad & \mathbf{K}(\boldsymbol{\rho}) \mathbf{U} = \mathbf{F}, \quad
\sum_{e=1}^N V_e \rho_e \le V^*, \quad
0 \le \rho_e \le 1,
\end{aligned}

with E_e(\rho_e) = E_{\min} + \rho_e^p (E_0 - E_{\min}), p \ge 3.

Theorem C.1 (KKT Conditions).
At a local optimum, there exist multipliers \lambda and \mu_e^\pm such that

\frac{\partial C}{\partial \rho_e} + \lambda V_e - \mu_e^- + \mu_e^+ = 0, \quad
\mu_e^- \rho_e = 0, \quad \mu_e^+(\rho_e - 1) = 0.

The stationarity condition yields the standard optimality criterion

\rho_e^{\text{new}} = \rho_e \left( -\frac{\partial C/\partial \rho_e}{\lambda V_e} \right)^{\!1/2},

where \partial C/\partial \rho_e = -p \rho_e^{p-1}(E_0 - E_{\min}) \mathbf{u}_e^\mathsf{T} \tilde{\mathbf{k}}_e \mathbf{u}_e.

