Appendix H: Robust Optimisation and Fault‑Tolerant Constraints

H.1 Uncertainty Set

The uncertainty set \Delta includes:

· Wind gusts up to 30 m s⁻¹ (Beaufort 8).
· Payload mass uncertainty ±5%.
· Terrain height variation ±10 cm.

H.2 Robust Constraint Formulation

All constraints g_j(\Psi, \delta) must hold for every \delta \in \Delta:

g_j(\Psi, \delta) \le 0 \quad \forall \delta \in \Delta.

In practice, the worst‑case combination is evaluated using a scenario approach or a first‑order reliability method.

H.3 Fault‑Tolerance Constraint (C10)

Let \Psi_{\setminus i} denote the morphology with leg i immobilised. The fault‑tolerance margin is

\text{FT}(\Psi) = \min_{i \in \{1,\dots,n_{\text{legs}}\}} \Omega_{\text{static}}(\Psi_{\setminus i}),

and the constraint reads \text{FT}(\Psi) \ge \Omega_{\text{crit}}. For a hexapod this is achievable; for a quadruped it is not, as shown in Theorem F.2.


